      "body": "## Motivation\n\nLarge JSON request bodies (for example base64-encoded multimodal inputs) can exceed default HTTP/1.1 parser limits in Uvicorn and Granian, causing failed requests before they reach application code. Issue #6622 asks for a server flag to raise this limit.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Add `--max-payload-size` to serving CLI arguments (default 10 MiB / 10485760 bytes).\n- Wire the limit into all HTTP server launch paths in `http_server.py` (Granian + Uvicorn, including multi-worker).\n- Document the flag in `server_arguments.mdx`.\n\nFixes #6622\n\nSigned-off-by: bantianyue <bantianyue@gmail.com>\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40666028127](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40666028127)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40666027954](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40666027954)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #40666028066](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40666028066)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
